{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning","id":976454,"title":"Temporal Summoning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T04:02:34-07:00","id":976454,"title":"Temporal Summoning","content":"<b>&quot;Temporal Summoning</b><br /> We are all the sum of our previous selves, and with this spell<br /> a mage can call those afterimages forth. Cast upon an object,<br /> area, or living being, this spell replaces its subject with an earlier<br /> version of itself, chosen by the caster. Without the Temporal<br /> Sympathy Attainment, only Unchanged pasts may be brought to<br /> the present, but this is still sufficient to remove most Conditions<br /> and heal injuries. By employing Temporal Sympathy, the mage<br /> can restore ancient ruins to their inhabited state, return her enemies<br /> to childhood, or even bring the dead back to life. When<br /> the spell\u2019s Duration ends, the subject immediately returns to its<br /> present self. Injuries, Conditions, and other effects imposed on<br /> the subject while Temporal Summoning is in effect transfer to<br /> the present version of the subject when it returns.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ok, I got the basis utility of the spell but how does it work in-game? For simplicity's sake lets assume that I target myself<br /> <br /> <b>1) &quot;...replaces subject with earlier version...&quot;</b><br /> a) So, if I replace me with my past self, will my injuries magicaly appear into my past self or do I just &quot;copy-paste&quot; my past pattern into the present? Is this a common occurance for Time mages to have scars and broken limbs appearing out of the blue?<br /> b) What about my memories? Do I maintain awareness of the situation for the duration of the spell or would I have the mindset of my past self? Will my past self realise that the injuries he received were from his future self?<br /> c) What if I target a temporal point before my awakening? Will my sleeper self cause dissonance to my own spell? How fast will the spell dissolve percieved by the <b>present</b> timeline.<br /> <br /> <b>2) &quot;...Without Temporal Sympathy Attainment, only Unchanged pasts may be brought to present...&quot;</b> and <b>&quot;Unchanged = Person not spoken to anyone, been anywhere since target time&quot;</b><br /> a) What's the point of using this spell without Temporal Sympathy Attainment? Any practical applications?<br /> <br /> 3) When how could anyone end my spell? Could it be counterspelled both in the past and the present? What would it take to end it without counterspell and prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T05:45:01-07:00","id":976480,"title":"","content":"Have you read the errata on the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:55:23-07:00","id":976585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;Temporal Summoning</b><br /> We are all the sum of our previous selves, and with this spell<br /> a mage can call those afterimages forth. Cast upon an object,<br /> area, or living being, this spell replaces its subject with an earlier<br /> version of itself, chosen by the caster. Without the Temporal<br /> Sympathy Attainment, only Unchanged pasts may be brought to<br /> the present, but this is still sufficient to remove most Conditions<br /> and heal injuries. By employing Temporal Sympathy, the mage<br /> can restore ancient ruins to their inhabited state, return her enemies<br /> to childhood, or even bring the dead back to life. When<br /> the spell\u2019s Duration ends, the subject immediately returns to its<br /> present self. Injuries, Conditions, and other effects imposed on<br /> the subject while Temporal Summoning is in effect transfer to<br /> the present version of the subject when it returns.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Note, this is the pre-errata version of the spell. The wording on the version in the <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9UUZ4UjZJdEhIM2c/view\" target=\"_blank\">errata document</a> is:<br /> <br /> &quot;We are all the sum of our previous selves, and with this spell a mage can call those afterimages forth. Cast upon an object, area, or living being, this spell replaces its subject with an earlier version of itself, chosen by the caster. Without the Temporal Sympathy Attainment, only Unchanged pasts may be brought to the present, but this is still sufficient to remove most Conditions and heal injuries. By employing Temporal Sympathy, the mage can restore ancient ruins to their inhabited state, or return her enemies to childhood. When the spell\u2019s Duration ends, the subject immediately returns to its present self. Injuries, Conditions, and other effects imposed on the subject while Temporal Summoning is in effect transfer to the present version of the subject when it returns. <b>The spell does have limits, however; it cannot bring the dead back to life or undo transformation into supernatural beings, though it still changes the subject physically - a vampire returned to &quot;childhood&quot; becomes a vampiric child, and a corpse stripped of decades becomes a younger-looking corpse with no cause of death.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of your questions still apply to the new version, but since you quoted the pre-errata version I thought you might not have seen the errata doc yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I got the basis utility of the spell but how does it work in-game? For simplicity's sake lets assume that I target myself<br /> <br /> <b>1) &quot;...replaces subject with earlier version...&quot;</b><br /> a) So, if I replace me with my past self, will my injuries magicaly appear into my past self or do I just &quot;copy-paste&quot; my past pattern into the present?</div> </div> </div> </div>You &quot;copy-paste&quot; your past pattern into the present. That's one of the main purposes of the spell, in fact; it's functionally a healing spell you can cast with Time instead of Life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a common occurance for Time mages to have scars and broken limbs appearing out of the blue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, but not because of Temporal Summoning. That's what it looks like to observers in the past when a Time Mage uses Shifting Sands or Corridors of Time on themselves <i>without</i> using Temporal Summoning first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b) What about my memories? Do I maintain awareness of the situation for the duration of the spell or would I have the mindset of my past self?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll retain your memories. You're effectively only replacing your physical body, not your mind (though maybe a Combined spell with the Mind Arcanum could do both).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will my past self realise that the injuries he received were from his future self?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your past self doesn't change, only your present self does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c) What if I target a temporal point before my awakening? Will my sleeper self cause dissonance to my own spell? How fast will the spell dissolve percieved by the <b>present</b> timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per the errata, your present form would change to match the age and appearance of your pre-Awakening self, but you would still be Awakened in the present. And since the spell doesn't actually change anything in the past, no, your past self doesn't trigger Dissonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>2) &quot;...Without Temporal Sympathy Attainment, only Unchanged pasts may be brought to present...&quot;</b> and <b>&quot;Unchanged = Person not spoken to anyone, been anywhere since target time&quot;</b><br /> <br /> a) What's the point of using this spell without Temporal Sympathy Attainment? Any practical applications?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned in the spell description, it might be sufficient to get rid of very recent injuries or Conditions. But generally speaking, yeah, you'll want to use this spell with Temporal Sympathy most of the time. Which shouldn't be too much of a problem, since you can't have enough dots in Time to cast this spell and not have Temporal Sympathy Attainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning#post976454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) When how could anyone end my spell? Could it be counterspelled both in the past and the present? What would it take to end it without counterspell and prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, only in the present. The spell doesn't do anything at all to or in the past, it just makes your present self into a copy of your past self. It could be countered normally or dispelled. I suppose another Time Mage could probably fuck with you by going back in time to a point before the point from which you drew your pattern to replace yourself and do beat the hell out of to you in the past, so that you would be replacing your present self with your beat-up past self. But that seems a lot more complicated than countering or dispelling it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:56:02-07:00","id":976586,"title":"","content":"Apparently I hadn't.<br /> <br /> Edited: Just, noticed you already answered in detail. Thank you, both, guys! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":".  Questions already answered 09-26-2016, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:30:51-07:00","id":976825,"title":"","content":"So the damage all comes back when the spell ends if you used it to patch up?<br /> Does healing progress on the present self while you're walking around with your past health?<br /> Otherwise, I guess it's good to keep a medic on standby for when the effect ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:35:19-07:00","id":976888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=976825#post976825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the damage all comes back when the spell ends if you used it to patch up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, unless you just cast it with indefinite duration and either give up on that spell control slot or spend the Willpower dot to relinquish it safely. Of course, if it gets dispelled...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=976825#post976825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does healing progress on the present self while you're walking around with your past health?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=976825#post976825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, I guess it's good to keep a medic on standby for when the effect ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's a good way to buy yourself enough time to <i>get to</i> a medic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T21:13:56-07:00","id":977589,"title":"","content":"I'm actually curious how <i>Unchanged</i> applies to an injured physical form. Hadn't noticed that until this thread. Looks like injury knocks the connection to <i>Strong</i>, the way I'm reading it, yet obviously that's not the interpretation of this.<br /> <br /> What's the dividing line? I get that there is grace to this, but how much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T22:22:48-07:00","id":977602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=977589#post977589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually curious how <i>Unchanged</i> applies to an injured physical form. Hadn't noticed that until this thread. Looks like injury knocks the connection to <i>Strong</i>, the way I'm reading it, yet obviously that's not the interpretation of this.<br /> <br /> What's the dividing line? I get that there is grace to this, but how much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't get it either tbh. I guess if you got hurt but you didn't leave the room or talk to anyone since getting hurt it counts as Unchanged still? \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:19:19-07:00","id":977622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=977602#post977602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't get it either tbh. I guess if you got hurt but you didn't leave the room or talk to anyone since getting hurt it counts as Unchanged still? \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Things that literally just happened&quot; is kind of necessarily a narrower field than any phrasing that includes the words &quot;intervening time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:25:04-07:00","id":977625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=977622#post977622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Things that literally just happened&amp;quot; is kind of necessarily a narrower field than any phrasing that includes the words &amp;quot;intervening time.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't Temporal Sympathy work based on how much the subject has changed, rather than how much time has passed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T00:18:30-07:00","id":977648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=977625#post977625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't Temporal Sympathy work based on how much the subject has changed, rather than how much time has passed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal Sympathy is using how much the subject has changed <i>as a measure of</i> &quot;how much&quot; time has passed. An injury can happen in the space of an instant, but healing takes <i>time</i>.<br /> <br /> Nitpicking about the particulars of Unchanged Sympathy <i>doesn't work</i> when Strong Sympathy <i>specifically lists</i> &quot;a person [\u2026] hours after an injury&quot; as an example.<br /> <br /> Remember what using the Attainment actually requires. Would you need a photograph of a person ten minutes ago to be able to say &quot;this guy had not yet been stabbed in the face&quot; and have him replace the guy who just got stabbed in the face ten seconds ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-28-2016, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:58:11-07:00","id":978016,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no sale.<br /> Sympathy is a link a specific pattern that distinguishes a pattern from any others. (In this case, through time)<br /> &quot;A person, hours after an injury&quot; represents a person whose injuries have had little time to heal.<br /> <br /> That's a far lesser change than <i>getting the injury</i>, so you're actually making a case for it being a <i>worse</i> level than Strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:36:20-07:00","id":978222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/976454-temporal-summoning?p=978016#post978016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a far lesser change than <i>getting the injury</i>, so you're actually making a case for it being a <i>worse</i> level than Strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corresponding Medium example is &quot;A person after a prolonged illness.&quot; Temporal Sympathy deals with the weight of a subject's <i>history</i> as a complicating factor. A wound you just got in the same scene is not quite temporally settled in the same fashion that a wound you got the morning of that day is.<br /> <br /> Stuff that happened very recently is the Time equivalent of sensory range; it's close to hand and doesn't need to engage with sympathy to the degree that warrants the Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-29-2016, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:47:46-07:00","id":978514,"title":"","content":"Now <i>that</i> <b>is</b> the beginning of a sound principle to play with:<br /> <br /> Events witnessed in a scene can be accounted for temporally <i>within that scene</i>. Use <i>Unchanged</i> sympathy to bridge witnessed changes within that window.<br /> After the scene, the change begins to pose a distraction to that link, requiring higher temporal sympathy as described by the charts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cool. Thanks Satchel &amp; Charlaquin. That helped settle things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}